From 9de4f0fc4ca5da211632c67072533cf21fa2f0a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abinash Haldorai <abinash.haldorai@eka.care>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:05:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Voice: answer a phone number by its integration, with the
 caller ID as a hint

Today the Vobiz answer URL names the agent (?agent_id=...), so pointing a
number at a different agent, or switching it off, means editing Vobiz.

Add POST /voice/answer/{integration_uuid}. The console registers a number
(channel telephony, provider vobiz) and binds it to an agent; matrix reads
that from the shared Postgres (integrations + product_integrations) and
answers with the bound agent. Unknown, unbound, paused, archived or
wrong-provider numbers get a 404 and no session, and the agent must belong
to the number's workspace (the binding API does not check that). The
integration uuid is the access control, as for WhatsApp numbers in doot.

The answer handler is split so both routes share the same call setup.

The caller ID that /answer already saved in the session context is now
given to the agent on phone calls, as an unverified hint in the existing
<USER_CONTEXT> shape with a note to confirm it. It is validated as a
phone number first, read only for sessions /answer created, and never sent
to tool servers as the user's identity. A signed-in user's mobile still
wins. WebRTC is untouched.

Register the answer helper in test_api_telemetry's _OUTCOME_IN_HELPER, as
the repo does for handlers that log through a helper.

Not tested against a real database or Vobiz account; the lookup is tested
with a mocked Postgres client.

